  "body": "## What changed\n\nA save to the project's own file now checks the file on disk first. The\nproject remembers the file's disk stamp (path, size, modification time)\nwhen it is opened and after each save. If the stamp is different at the\nnext save, the file on disk changed after the open or the last save:\n\n- The window holds the save and asks: **Save As**, **Cancel** or\n  **Overwrite**. Nothing is written before the answer.\n- `cam.save` and the MCP tool `save_project` refuse by name. The refusal\n  names the file and `overwrite: true`. `save_project` has a new optional\n  argument `overwrite`. `cam.save` has a new options object:\n  `cam.save(path?, { overwrite?: boolean })`.\n- An agent attached to the window uses the window's stamp. The live seam\n  takes it in (`LiveOptions::doc_stamp`) and gives the new stamp back\n  (`LiveAnswer::doc_stamp`), so the window does not ask about the\n  agent's own save.\n\nA save to another path, a new document and a file that was deleted are\nnot checked. The stamp of our own save replaces the old stamp, so the\nnext save does not ask. In the window, New and Open drop the old stamp\nand a held save, so a held save never writes another document.\n\n- The stamp is `project::DiskStamp`, beside `project::save` and\n  `project::load`. The checks are `script::save_guard::check` and\n  `State::may_save_over`.\n  `project::save`, the file format and `PROJECT_VERSION` do not change.\n- Behaviour change: a script or an agent that saved over a changed file\n  is now refused. It must pass `overwrite: true`.\n- The behaviour matches SolidCraft's overwrite guard. The texts are\n  CamCraft's own.\n- `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and `assets/scripts/cam.d.ts` are updated for\n  the new argument. The MCP and CLI guide pages have one paragraph each.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3608-save-overwrite-guard.md`.\n\nThis branch starts at upstream/main `60b19abe8`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew in `crates/app/tests/save_overwrite_guard.rs`:\n\n- `a_stamp_sees_a_foreign_write_but_not_a_missing_file_or_another_path`\n- `an_mcp_save_over_a_changed_file_is_refused_until_overwrite`\n- `an_mcp_open_stamps_the_file`\n- `a_save_to_another_path_or_over_a_deleted_file_is_not_refused`\n- `a_bad_save_option_is_refused_by_name_and_writes_nothing`\n- `a_script_save_over_a_changed_file_is_refused_until_overwrite`\n- `an_attached_agent_save_meets_the_window_stamp_and_hands_back_the_new_one`\n\nNew in `crates/ui/src/save_guard_tests.rs`:\n\n- `a_save_over_a_changed_file_asks_and_overwrite_replaces_it`\n- `cancel_keeps_the_file_and_save_as_goes_to_the_save_as_dialog`\n- `the_window_s_own_saves_never_ask`\n- `a_save_to_another_file_or_over_a_deleted_file_does_not_ask`\n- `a_held_save_from_the_unsaved_prompt_keeps_the_document_open`\n- `a_new_document_drops_a_held_save`\n\nNew layout test: `layout_window_overwrite_prompt`\n(`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/page_layout_windows.rs`).\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` (Windows 11): 216 steps, 214 passed, 2 failed,\n0 stalled. It ran the app and ui libs (ui lib: 1480 passed, the new tests\nand the layout test among them), `save_overwrite_guard` (7 passed),\n`mcp_live`, `mcp_doc_drift`, `scripting`, every app suite that names\n`app::project`, `app::script` or `mcp (tools)`, and 16 ui suites.\nThe 2 failed steps do not touch this change:\n\n- `first_part_programs::first_router_part_posts_the_shipped_program`\n  fails on upstream/main `60b19abe8` (#3574, main is red).\n- `example_catalog::catalog_2d_drill_overfeed::{rebuilds,regenerates}`\n  differs only by line ends: this Windows checkout (`core.autocrlf=true`)\n  turns the LF file `examples/catalog/2d/drill-overfeed/refusal.txt`\n  into CRLF.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\nThe gate and clippy ran on this change before the issue existed. The head\ndiffers from that tree only in the issue number: in code comments and in\nthe name of the decision file.\nHeavy lanes: not run. The change is not under the safety floor (no\nposted G-code, collision check, simulation or geometry), so no targeted\nheavy step applies (#3556).\nReach from `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run`: \"app heavy: every target\"\n(212 steps), because `crates/app/src/mcp/live.rs` changed. Not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The window's step that keeps an agent's new stamp (`mcp_host.rs`, three\n  lines). The app test pins the stamp that the live seam gives back. The\n  AI chat's Allow path is not driven in a test.\n- The prompt's buttons by a click. The tests call\n  `actions::resolve_overwrite`, and the layout test checks the modal.\n- Save As after the prompt: it opens the system file dialog. The test\n  checks that the Save As command is queued.\n- A write that keeps the size and the modification time. Some file systems\n  keep the time in steps of 1 or 2 seconds. This is a known limit.\n- Two real CamCraft processes, git, a sync client and a network share. A\n  plain write of other bytes stands in for each.\n- Linux and macOS.\n\nChangelog: Saving a project no longer silently writes over changes that another window, program or person saved to the same file.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3608\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
